[h1]Brotato Online Friends[/h1]

This Mod is an unofficial, independently maintained fork of Brotato Online by six666, supporting Steam and LAN multiplayer. It focuses on improving shop actions, weapon upgrades, retries and wave settlement, and allows multiple local players to join from one client.

Designed for cooperative play between trusted friends, rather than anti-cheat enforcement. More responsive client actions and more reliable synchronization.

[b]Current version:[/b] 6.8.5
[b]Game version targeted by this update:[/b] 1.2.0.2
[b]Original author:[/b] six666
[b]Fork maintainer:[/b] wushuangabao
[b]Mod ID:[/b] wushuangabao-BrotatoOnlineFriends

[h2]Main Features[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Immediate personal shop actions[/b]
Purchases, rerolls, locks, weapon combinations, recycling, dismantling and mechanization execute locally, then synchronize their results, reducing delays caused by waiting for host replies.

[*][b]Multiple players on one client[/b]
Clients support multiple input devices: keyboard/mouse plus controllers, or multiple controllers. For example, one host player plus two client players, or two players on each side.

[*][b]Complete personal-state synchronization before combat[/b]
Prevents entering combat before the final purchase or upgrade has synchronized.

[*][b]More reliable retries and battle entry[/b]
Fixes clients failing to re-enter combat after retrying a failed wave, and lets late clients automatically enter after the host starts.

[*][b]Client rewards and statistics[/b]
Fixes lost in-run rewards for characters such as Hiker. Display-only character statistics are synchronized at the end of each wave.

[*][b]Equipment effects and linked statistics[/b]
Synchronizes effects after weapon purchases, combinations and recycling, preventing lingering structure bonuses. Preserves nested effect data such as flame turrets for vanilla characters and Mods using native effects.

[*][b]Consistent crate rewards and mutations[/b]
The host applies crate rewards and synchronizes the resulting items, mutations, tumor and evolution. Clients do not reroll mutations, and weapon combinations from crates synchronize correctly when all weapon slots are occupied.

[*][b]Full-health pickups respect the wave limit[/b]
Remote full-health pickups grant only the remaining allowance for the wave. Attributes, item tracking and wave counters use the same actual gain, preventing excess rewards.

[*][b]Complete local wave settlement[/b]
When the host reaches the shop first, clients finish local settlement before synchronizing the scene transition, preserving local callbacks and progress records.
[/list]

[h2]How to Use[/h2]

[list]
[*]Disable other multiplayer Mods. The host and every client should subscribe to the same 6.8.5 version. Fully exit and restart the game after updating.
[*]Join the same room through a Steam lobby or LAN.
[*]To add local players on a client, hold the join button on each additional device while on the character selection screen.
[*]Additional players can join only before the run starts. The room supports four players total.
[*]For keyboard/mouse plus controllers, first set the first player’s online input device to keyboard/mouse.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility and Notes[/h2]

[list]
[*]This update targets game version 1.2.0.2. The host and clients must use the same game version. Older game versions were not tested in this validation.
[*]This version uses network protocol 6.5.4. Crate rewards now synchronize the host's final result, so every player must update to 6.8.5. It cannot connect with 6.8.4 or earlier releases.
[*]The protocol update does not change the save format or invalidate existing saves simply because the protocol version changed.
[*]6.8.1 network co-op saves can be continued; keep the save and identity files. Data from the original six666-BrotatoOnline ID is not migrated automatically.
[*]Not all character, item and third-party Mod combinations have been verified.
[/list]

[h2]Version History[/h2]

The following summarizes this branch’s development. Some versions were development builds rather than separate Workshop releases.

[list]
[*][b]6.6.6 | Original Foundation[/b]
The starting point for this fork, retaining the original Brotato Online multiplayer framework and cooperative flow.

[*][b]6.6.7 | Shop Synchronization, Retries and Automatic Entry[/b]
Fixed host shop actions failing to synchronize while paused and retry scene reloads being blocked by deduplication. Added start-message retries and late-client recovery to prevent clients remaining in an old scene.

[*][b]6.6.8 | Locked Offers and Purchased-Weapon Recovery[/b]
Fixed locked client offers becoming impossible to unlock or purchase, and older combine results overwriting newly purchased weapons. Added state recovery and protection against delayed messages, avoiding duplicate purchases or charges.

[*][b]6.7.0 | Client Local Co-op[/b]
Allowed multiple input devices to join as separate players on one client, with independent character selection, shopping, movement, damage and death. Extended ownership, reconnection and related interactions to multiple local players.

[*][b]6.8.0 | Independent Friends Edition and Local Shops[/b]
Switched to a separate Mod ID. Personal shop actions execute locally and synchronize their results, with complete personal-state handoff before combat. Fixed unresponsive mechanical upgrades, incorrect weapon matching, delayed messages closing popups and focus jumping between slots.

[*][b]6.8.1 | Wave Settlement and Steam Initialization[/b]
Fixed skipped client settlement when the host entered the shop first, and added synchronization of the leftover-material ledger. Reused already initialized Steam instances to fix the Steam.run_callbacks duplicate-connection error at startup.

[*][b]6.8.2 | Selection Input and Saved Runs[/b]
Fixes hidden character lists, extra join panels, local input affecting remote seats, and restored client seats ignoring a second controller in favor of the keyboard. Undiagnosed physical hotplug swaps have not been changed.

[*][b]6.8.3 | Client Rewards and Generic Statistics[/b]
Fixes lost or duplicated movement rewards, stale data overwriting actual maximum health, and missing custom statistics or array values. Adds same-attempt rejoin recovery, retry rollback and final-record waiting.

[*][b]6.8.4 | Equipment Effects and Linked Statistics[/b]
Fixes detached equipment-effect references, stale item counts and linked statistics, and missing nested flame-turret data. Also fixes growing description arguments and duplicated native subeffects, including Seashell, Javelin and Builder effects.

[*][b]6.8.5 | Game 1.2.0.2 Compatibility[/b]
Fixes clients rerolling crate mutations and remote full-health pickups exceeding the wave limit. Protects inventory synchronization against duplicate or outdated crate messages and during endless-mode shop transitions. Network protocol increases to 6.5.4, requiring every player to update; the save format is unchanged.
[/list]

